---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NoteRow from '../components/NoteRow.astro';
const notes = (await getCollection('notes')).sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span>A public notebook for figuring things out</p>
      <h1>Learning,<br /><em>out loud.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-intro">I’m Sahil. I’m turning the things I study into notes, small experiments, and explanations I can return to. Right now: neural networks from scratch. Next: wherever curiosity leads.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button-primary" href={`${base}lab/`}>Explore the neural net lab <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}notebooks/micrograd/`}>Read the notebook <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}notes/`}>Read the notes <span>→</span></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-label="An abstract graph of a curve approximated by a neural network" role="img">
      <div class="art-label art-label-top">THE CURRENT QUESTION</div>
      <div class="art-question">Can a tiny network<br />learn this curve?</div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 480 360" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <g class="art-grid"><path d="M0 60H480M0 120H480M0 180H480M0 240H480M0 300H480M80 0V360M160 0V360M240 0V360M320 0V360M400 0V360" /></g>
        <path class="art-curve-shadow" d="M25 55 C100 252 120 305 218 310 C320 313 372 215 455 45" />
        <path class="art-curve" d="M25 55 C100 252 120 305 218 310 C320 313 372 215 455 45" />
        <path class="art-prediction" d="M25 125 C100 175 145 279 218 268 C315 251 360 195 455 103" />
      </svg>
      <div class="art-legend"><span><i class="legend-target"></i> target function</span><span><i class="legend-learned"></i> network prediction</span></div>
      <div class="art-bottom"><span>01 / MICROGRAD</span><span>LEARNING IN PROGRESS <b>●</b></span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-band"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><p class="section-kicker">The idea</p><h2>Collect the questions.<br /><span>Show the working.</span></h2><p>This is a record of learning in motion: what clicked, what didn’t, and what happened when I tried it in code. Each subject gets notes and experiments of its own.</p></div></section>

  <section class="current-section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Currently exploring</p><h2>Neural networks<br /><em>from the inside out.</em></h2></div><p>Starting with Karpathy’s micrograd lecture and my own notebook, then building a browser experiment that makes training visible.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><a class="feature-card feature-card-dark" href={`${base}lab/`}><div class="feature-top"><span>INTERACTIVE EXPERIMENT</span><span>↗</span></div><div class="feature-signal" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><div><h3>Watch the weights change</h3><p>Write a function, build a network, and select a neuron to see its weights update as it trains.</p></div></a><a class="feature-card feature-card-light" href={`${base}notes/starting-with-micrograd/`}><div class="feature-top"><span>FIELD NOTE 001</span><span>↗</span></div><div class="feature-formula" aria-hidden="true">∂L<span>/</span>∂w</div><div><h3>Starting with micrograd</h3><p>From numerical derivatives to a tiny autograd engine, neurons, layers, and gradient descent.</p></div></a></div></section>

  <section class="notes-section wrap"><div class="notes-header"><div><p class="section-kicker">The journal</p><h2>Recent notes</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}notes/`}>View all notes <span>→</span></a></div><div class="note-list">{notes.slice(0, 3).map((note) => <NoteRow note={note} />)}</div><p class="notes-outro">More subjects will appear here as I learn them. No need to have it all figured out first.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
